  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Sheherezade is a large format flipbook by Janet Zweig that features, on one side, a small illustration of a woman repeatedly putting on a cape, and on the other, a text by Holly Anderson that gradually recedes into the gaps of larger photographic images of printed text, which themselves become smaller and resolve themselves into readable stories only to recede into the gaps of a larger text... The story continues to unfold and disappear in this visual interpretation of the story of Sheherazade in The Thousand and One Nights. Each book is Smythe sewn and bound in Strathmore Grandee covers with gold stamping." -- Printed Matter website, accessed 4/26/2012.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Printed by Carl Sesto, Newburyport, MA., bound by Mueller Trade Bindery, Middletown, CT., available from Sheherezade...Long Island City, NY."</subfield>
